<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd">

    <!--
      DB-generated UUID primary key — the org-wide migration EXEMPLAR.

      Decision (pinned): stop minting UUID primary keys in Java
      (UUID.randomUUID()); let Postgres generate them via a column DEFAULT of
      gen_random_uuid() (UUIDv4, from the pgcrypto extension — the most-secure
      PG-native UUID generator) and read the generated id back on insert. The
      column type stays uuid and the entity @Id stays java.util.UUID; only the
      SOURCE of the id moves from the app to the database.

      mod_action.id is ALREADY a native uuid PK (changelog 001) — so there is NO
      type migration here. This changeset only:

        1. CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pgcrypto — provides gen_random_uuid().
           Idempotent + harmless if already present (other HugMesh schemas
           install it too). This is the reason the affected slice tests move to
           Testcontainers-Postgres: H2 has neither pgcrypto nor a reliable
           INSERT ... RETURNING, so the prod changelog can no longer be applied
           over the H2 PostgreSQL-compat store.

        2. ADD a DEFAULT of gen_random_uuid() to mod_action.id. After this, an
           INSERT that OMITS id gets a DB-generated UUIDv4; the repository's
           INSERT ... RETURNING id reads the generated value back.

      Numbered 009, one above the current max (008-mod-action-notify). Appended
      LAST in the master changelog.
    -->

    <changeSet id="009-pgcrypto-extension" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>Install pgcrypto so gen_random_uuid() is available as the
                 mod_action.id column DEFAULT. IF NOT EXISTS — idempotent.</comment>
        <sql>CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pgcrypto;</sql>
    </changeSet>

    <changeSet id="009-mod-action-id-db-default" author="hugmesh">
        <comment>Let the database generate mod_action.id via gen_random_uuid()
                 (UUIDv4) instead of the app minting UUID.randomUUID(). The
                 column stays uuid PK; only the id SOURCE moves to the DB. The
                 repository INSERTs now omit id and RETURNING id reads it back.</comment>
        <addDefaultValue tableName="mod_action"
                         columnName="id"
                         columnDataType="uuid"
                         defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
